1
00:00:02,700 --> 00:00:05,740
One morning, Phanith is riding to work as usual.

2
00:00:05,740 --> 00:00:09,350
Suddenly — bang! A tire bursts in the middle of the road.

3
00:00:09,350 --> 00:00:14,220
There is no repair shop anywhere around, and Phanith doesn't know what to do.

4
00:00:15,520 --> 00:00:18,420
But then Phanith remembers the HRC app.

5
00:00:18,420 --> 00:00:21,610
Phanith opens the phone and taps "Help me".

6
00:00:21,610 --> 00:00:25,480
In just a few minutes, the nearest mechanic arrives.

7
00:00:25,480 --> 00:00:28,900
Fixed, with a clear price and an easy payment.

8
00:00:28,900 --> 00:00:34,840
Phanith rides on safely. Help Road Cambodia — roadside help, any time, anywhere.

9
00:00:38,540 --> 00:00:42,590
Hello! I'm HRC, the assistant of Help Road Cambodia.

10
00:00:42,590 --> 00:00:51,080
When your motorbike or car breaks down on the road, the HRC app brings the nearest mechanic to where you are.

11
00:00:51,080 --> 00:01:00,660
In this video I'll show you, step by step, how to use the customer app — from signing up to paying and rating the mechanic.

12
00:01:01,960 --> 00:01:05,280
Before we start, let's look at the whole process.

13
00:01:05,280 --> 00:01:11,860
One: sign up with your phone number. Two: request help by choosing the problem and your location.

14
00:01:11,860 --> 00:01:15,310
Three: a mechanic accepts the job and comes to you.

15
00:01:15,310 --> 00:01:19,860
Four: the mechanic checks and repairs after you agree to the price.

16
00:01:19,860 --> 00:01:23,720
Five: pay by KHQR or in cash. And six: rate the mechanic.

17
00:01:25,170 --> 00:01:30,300
Step one: install the HRC app on your phone and open it.

18
00:01:30,300 --> 00:01:34,860
The intro screens show what the app can do — tap "Continue".

19
00:01:34,860 --> 00:01:41,440
Then allow the app to use your location, so the mechanic can find you and the distance fee is correct.

20
00:01:41,440 --> 00:01:45,860
And allow notifications, so you know right away when a mechanic accepts or arrives.

21
00:01:47,160 --> 00:01:52,270
Next, sign in. Enter your phone number and tap "Get OTP code".

22
00:01:52,270 --> 00:01:55,900
You will receive an SMS with a 6-digit code.

23
00:01:55,900 --> 00:02:04,480
Type the code, then tap "Verify". If you use a foreign phone number, you can also sign in with Telegram.

24
00:02:05,930 --> 00:02:08,750
The first time you sign in, fill in a few details.

25
00:02:08,750 --> 00:02:13,580
Type your name and choose the vehicle you use most: motorbike, tuk-tuk or car.

26
00:02:13,580 --> 00:02:17,220
Tick to accept the terms of use, then tap "Start".

27
00:02:18,520 --> 00:02:24,590
This is the home screen. The big orange "Help me" button in the middle calls the mechanic nearest to you.

28
00:02:24,590 --> 00:02:29,850
Below are the quick services — tire, engine, fuel and tow — that you can tap straight away.

29
00:02:29,850 --> 00:02:33,850
The badge at the top tells you whether day or night prices apply now.

30
00:02:33,850 --> 00:02:37,720
And the bar at the bottom takes you to History, Alerts and Account.

31
00:02:39,020 --> 00:02:43,110
When you tap "Help me", the "Request help" page opens with three steps.

32
00:02:43,110 --> 00:02:50,890
First, choose your vehicle. Then choose the problem, such as a flat tire, an inner tube change, an engine that won't start, or no fuel.

33
00:02:50,890 --> 00:02:53,940
Each service shows its starting price under its name.

34
00:02:53,940 --> 00:02:54,860
Then tap "Next".

35
00:02:56,160 --> 00:02:58,820
The third step is to confirm your location.

36
00:02:58,820 --> 00:03:02,110
The app uses GPS to put the orange pin where you are.

37
00:03:02,110 --> 00:03:11,090
You can write a note for the mechanic, for example "in front of the pagoda" or "next to the fuel station", and you can take a photo of the place.

38
00:03:11,090 --> 00:03:17,160
Then tap "Confirm location". Note that the service works only inside the areas where HRC operates.

39
00:03:18,610 --> 00:03:21,820
Before you call a mechanic, you see a clear price estimate.

40
00:03:21,820 --> 00:03:29,340
This box shows the most you will pay for the service — for example, a motorbike tire patch by day costs no more than $4.50.

41
00:03:29,340 --> 00:03:37,100
The starting price includes 5 km of distance; parts are not included, and the mechanic must ask for your approval first.

42
00:03:37,100 --> 00:03:41,150
You can switch the payment method between cash and KHQR.

43
00:03:41,150 --> 00:03:43,100
When ready, tap "Call a mechanic now".

44
00:03:44,550 --> 00:03:48,150
Now the system is looking for the mechanic nearest to you.

45
00:03:48,150 --> 00:03:54,840
Each mechanic has 30 seconds to accept the job; if they don't, the system automatically offers it to the next one.

46
00:03:54,840 --> 00:03:58,160
While it is searching, you can cancel for free.

47
00:03:59,610 --> 00:04:04,710
When a mechanic accepts, you see their name, rating and verified badge.

48
00:04:04,710 --> 00:04:09,910
On the map you can follow the mechanic on the way and the estimated arrival time.

49
00:04:09,910 --> 00:04:12,940
Tap "Call" or "Chat" to talk to the mechanic.

50
00:04:12,940 --> 00:04:18,100
And the "Tell family" button lets you share this trip with your loved ones.

51
00:04:19,400 --> 00:04:25,210
When the mechanic arrives, they take a photo before the repair, to protect both you and the mechanic.

52
00:04:25,210 --> 00:04:28,660
If parts are needed, the mechanic sends you a price request.

53
00:04:28,660 --> 00:04:32,800
You see the photo, the reason, the price of each part and the new total.

54
00:04:32,800 --> 00:04:36,770
If you agree, tap "Approve". If not, tap "Decline" and give a reason.

55
00:04:36,770 --> 00:04:39,880
The mechanic cannot change any part until you approve.

56
00:04:41,330 --> 00:04:43,580
When the repair is done, it's time to pay.

57
00:04:43,580 --> 00:04:50,440
If you chose KHQR, scan this QR code with ABA or any other bank.

58
00:04:50,440 --> 00:04:54,830
You can also save the QR or tap "Open bank app".

59
00:04:54,830 --> 00:04:57,530
The system confirms the payment automatically.

60
00:04:57,530 --> 00:05:02,140
If you pay in cash, hand the money to the mechanic, and the mechanic confirms it in the app.

61
00:05:03,590 --> 00:05:06,000
The last step is to rate the mechanic.

62
00:05:06,000 --> 00:05:13,890
Tap one to five stars, pick what was good, such as "fast" or "polite", add a comment if you like, then tap "Submit rating".

63
00:05:13,890 --> 00:05:19,520
You then get a receipt with photos before and after the repair, and the full price details.

64
00:05:19,520 --> 00:05:24,200
You can download it as a PDF, or report a problem if something is wrong.

65
00:05:25,500 --> 00:05:32,840
Want to cancel a request? You can cancel for free while the system is searching, or within 2 minutes after a mechanic accepts.

66
00:05:32,840 --> 00:05:40,120
After that, or once the mechanic has arrived, a small cancellation fee may apply, and it is shown clearly before you confirm.

67
00:05:40,120 --> 00:05:44,140
This money goes to the mechanic for the time spent travelling to you.

68
00:05:45,440 --> 00:05:54,410
Your safety comes first. In an emergency, open the Emergency page and hold the red SOS button for 2 seconds.

69
00:05:54,410 --> 00:06:02,140
The HRC team and your emergency contacts receive your location, and HRC calls you right away.

70
00:06:02,140 --> 00:06:09,200
You can also call the police on 117, an ambulance on 119, or the fire service on 118.

71
00:06:10,650 --> 00:06:16,200
In the History tab you can see every job you have requested, with its price and status.

72
00:06:16,200 --> 00:06:20,770
Tap any job to see the details and the receipt, or to report a problem.

73
00:06:20,770 --> 00:06:29,260
And if you need help, go to Account, then Help, to read the common questions or call the HRC hotline, open 24 hours a day.

74
00:06:30,560 --> 00:06:41,220
To sum up, using the HRC app takes just six steps: sign up, request help, wait for the mechanic, agree to the price and repair, pay, and rate.

75
00:06:41,220 --> 00:06:48,200
Remember: the price is always shown first, and no part is ever changed without your approval.

76
00:06:49,500 --> 00:06:56,850
Thank you for watching! Whenever you have trouble on the road, just open the app and tap "Help me".

77
00:06:56,850 --> 00:07:00,200
HRC is here to help you — any time, anywhere.

78
00:07:00,200 --> 00:07:00,940
Ride safe!
